---
// MARKET BODY COPY — the depth pass (team call, 2026-08-18).
//
// THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. The layout was right and the market landings were the thinnest pages on
// the site at roughly 700 words of body text — thinner than the service hubs they route to. A page
// that routes well and says little is a page that ranks for nothing and gets skimmed by the reader
// it did reach.
//
// THE HARD REQUIREMENT, AND WHY IT SHAPED THE COPY RATHER THAN DECORATED IT. No market page may be
// another market page with the city swapped. That exact pattern — identical municipality copy
// across Cincinnati and St. Louis — is the diagnosed cause of the old site's collapse, so this
// content is not a template with `{city}` in it. Each market's blocks are written from its own
// climate, its own housing stock and its own communities:
//
//   Cincinnati  river-valley freeze-thaw, hillside drainage, pre-war brick and frame
//   Columbus    open flat ground and wind, 1990s-2000s suburban builds, ice damming
//   St. Louis   humidity and hail, and a brick housing stock almost unique in the Midwest
//
// Nothing here is interchangeable. Swapping the city name into another market's blocks would
// produce sentences that are factually wrong, which is the test the old site failed.
//
// MOBILE FIRST — 85/15. Short blocks with their own subheads rather than one wall of text: at
// 390px a reader scans subheads and stops where it is relevant. Paragraphs are capped near 60ch so
// a line does not run the full width of a phone.
//
// KEYWORDS ARE NOT STUFFED. If "roof replacement {city}" does not read as a sentence, it is not
// written as one. Every town named is in that market's `servedAreas` — no coverage is implied that
// the data does not carry.
//
// CLAIMS: nothing here asserts a timeframe, a price, a warranty beyond the approved 25-year
// workmanship one, a rating or a certification. See claims.js for why.
const { market, depth } = Astro.props;
const show = depth?.blocks?.length > 0;
---
{show && (
  <section class="mdepth" aria-labelledby={`mdepth-${market.slug}`}>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead">
        <span class="eyebrow">{depth.eyebrow ?? `Working on ${market.region} homes`}</span>
        <h2 id={`mdepth-${market.slug}`}>{depth.heading}</h2>
        {depth.intro && <p>{depth.intro}</p>}
      </div>
      <div class="mdepth-blocks" data-reveal="stagger">
        {depth.blocks.map((b) => (
          <article class="mdepth-block">
            <h3>{b.h}</h3>
            {b.p.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
